  data: {
    LLM: "After the deal, the first player to dealer's left may post a blind (fare il buio). Others then call, fold, or raise in poker fashion. If two or more remain, play starts: each turn a player draws one card from the stock or the top of the discard pile, then discards one card face up. A player may go out after drawing by laying 10 cards in sets (three or more of same rank) and runs (three or more consecutive same suit; Ace may be high or low). No melds are shown until going out. Jokers are wild. The winner takes the pool.",
    Player: "After the deal, the first player to dealer's left may post a blind (fare il buio). Others then call, fold, or raise in poker fashion. If two or more remain, play starts: each turn a player draws one card from the stock or the top of the discard pile, then discards one card face up. A player may go out after drawing by laying 10 cards in sets (three or more of same rank) and runs (three or more consecutive same suit; Ace may be high or low). No melds are shown until going out. Jokers are wild. The winner takes the pool.",
    objective: 'Win the hand by being first to go out with 10 cards in valid sets and runs and one discard, and collect the pool; or win the betting round when all others fold.',
    gameplay: "After the deal, the first player to dealer's left may post a blind (fare il buio). Others then call, fold, or raise in poker fashion. If two or more remain, play starts: each turn a player draws one card from the stock or the top of the discard pile, then discards one card face up. A player may go out after drawing by laying 10 cards in sets (three or more of same rank) and runs (three or more consecutive same suit; Ace may be high or low). No melds are shown until going out. Jokers are wild. The winner takes the pool.",
    keyRules: [
      'Sets are three or more cards of the same rank; runs are three or more consecutive cards of the same suit; Ace may be next to King or Two.',
      'First player may post a blind before looking; others call, fold, or raise. If only one remains after betting, that player wins the pool without play.',
      'Each turn: draw one from stock or top discard, then discard one. Going out: expose 10 cards in valid combinations and discard the 11th.',
      'Special hands (e.g. one 10-card run without Jokers) may entitle the winner to extra payments from active players.',
